-- title:
--   Étale fibre of B/k[X] at an unramified irreducible h
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $B$ be a commutative ring (in the same universe) which is a Dedekind domain, equipped with a $k[X]$-algebra structure and a $k$-algebra structure compatible with the inclusion $k \subseteq k[X]$, such that $B$ is finite as a $k[X]$-module and has no zero smul divisors over $k[X]$ (so that $k[X] \to B$ is injective). Let $h \in k[X]$ be irreducible and separable. Assume that for every prime ideal $P$ of $B$ with $P \neq \bot$ whose contraction $P \cap k[X]$ along $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ k[X]\ B$ contains the ideal $(h)$ — that is, every nonzero prime of $B$ lying over $(h)$ — the algebra $B$ over $k[X]$ is unramified at $P$ in the sense of `Algebra.IsUnramifiedAt k[X] P`, i.e. the localisation of $B$ at $P$ is formally unramified over $k[X]$. Then the quotient of $B$ by the ideal generated by the image of $(h)$, namely $B/hB$, is an étale $k$-algebra: it is formally étale over $k$ and of finite presentation over $k$.
--
--   This is the statement that the fibre over a closed point $(h)$ of the finite map $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \mathbb{A}^1_k$ is an étale $k$-algebra, provided the point is unramified and its residue field is separable over $k$; classically one writes $hB = \prod P$ with all ramification indices $1$ and obtains $B/hB \cong \prod_P \kappa(P)$ with each $\kappa(P)$ finite separable over $k$. It is used by the variant [`IsDedekindDomain.etale_quotient_map_span_of_separable_of_forall_isUnramifiedAt`](thm.html#IsDedekindDomain.etale_quotient_map_span_of_separable_of_forall_isUnramifiedAt) and, in the construction of level rings for modular curves, by [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_forall_etale_rat_tensorProduct_quotient_span_aeval_jChartFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_forall_etale_rat_tensorProduct_quotient_span_aeval_jChartFin).
